  "solution": {
    "text": "Total number of 5-digit numbers having all the digits distinct $={ }^{10} \\mathrm{P}_{5}-{ }^{9} \\mathrm{P}_{4}$\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{array}{l}\r\n=\\frac{10 !}{5 !}-\\frac{91}{5 !}=\\frac{10 \\times 9 !}{5 !}-\\frac{91}{51} \\\\\r\n=\\frac{91}{51}(10-1)=9 \\times \\frac{9!}{(9-4) !} \\\\\r\n=9 \\times 9 P_{4}\r\n\\end{array}\r\n$$",
